            "typeClass": "compound",
            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "The data contains raw records of the two surveys related to the setup of Collaborative Community Projects (CCPs) within the research project BOLSTER - Bridging Organizations and marginalized communities for Local Sustainablity Transitions in EuRope. Within the scheme of CCPs, local stakeholders were allowed to pilot-test their ideas for bottom-up “green” community actions co-financed by BOLSTER up to EUR 10000. The CCPs were organised in seven regions: Halle (DE), Silesia (PL), Istria (HR), Prahova (RO), Leon (ES), Stara Zagora (BG), Hainaut (BE).\nOne survey was targeting project partners in all seven regions – to receive CCPs descriptions. The other was addressed to the leaders of the CCPs, as BOLSTER researchers wanted to discover patterns that govern local leadership in environmental actions.<br><br>\nDue to the sensitivity of the data, they are not stored in DataverseNL but in a secure location at Tilburg University. If you would like to request access to the data file(s), please use the Contact Owner button on the dataset’s landing page."
                },
                "dsDescriptionDate": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionDate",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "2025-08-15"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
